Android's cRCompletion::UnInit (00061740) pays what a skipped delivery tally has
left through ScoreAdd, so the level bonus still meets the 50,000-point extra life
check. Windows passes the bonus as the score kind, worth nothing, then sets the
total directly (docs/port/original-bugs.md). Android's cRSubGoldy::AI (0007ac54)
holds the replay cursor and sample count while the summary waits for a click, so
an idle summary never reaches Time's Up.

